#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# covariance

#% text
# `covariance(xs, ys)` gives the sample covariance of two lists of the same length, `sum((xs - mean(xs))*conjugate(ys - mean(ys)))/(n - 1)`; exact for exact input. `covariance(m)` gives the matrix of covariances of the columns of the matrix `m`, and `covariance(m1, m2)` the covariances of the columns of `m1` against those of `m2`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
covariance([1, 3/2], [2, 11])
#% output
#= 9/4

#% cell
covariance([1.5, 3, 5, 10], [2, 1.25, 15, 8])
#% output
#= 11.260416666666666

#% cell
covariance([2 + im, 3 - 2im, 5 + 4im], [im, 1 + 2im, 10 - 5im])
#% output
#= -7/3 + 56*im/3

#% cell
covariance(identity_matrix(3))
#% output
#= [[1/3, -1/6, -1/6], [-1/6, 1/3, -1/6], [-1/6, -1/6, 1/3]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `correlation`, `variance`, `mean`
